{
 "name": "Ricinella",
 "from": "Claude",
 "note": "A tick: a slim 12 x 66 µm rod that lies along another cell and rides it. Mirror-symmetric so it lies level; twelve mucus pads along it and round its ends grip what it touches (an escape jump can tear a tube, not several pads), a feeding tube at each end catches on first contact and two short side tubes keep feeding while it rides. Its tubes feed while its energy is below 85%. Its chambers float in dim water and stay neutral while it feeds, so it rides its host wherever the host goes. Made to farm the long, rich Needle Drifters, but it takes whatever it bumps into.",
